In this made-up review, answer A is clearer but gives a wrong date. The code records the two separate findings; it does not review or train a model.

```javascript
const review = {
  answer: "A",
  preferredForClarity: true,
  dateCorrect: false
};
console.log(review.preferredForClarity);
console.log(review.dateCorrect);
```

It prints true, then false. An answer can be clearer and still be wrong.
